# Author Mermaid & presentations

Your expressive surface — how you emit capturable VISUAL artifacts (diagrams, slides) instead of walls of
text. Composes the `presentation` toolkit rather than re-implementing it.

**When to use:** you need to communicate something structural or sequential — an architecture, a flow, a
plan, a deck — where a diagram or slides land harder than prose.

## What you produce
- **Mermaid diagrams** — flowcharts, sequences, graphs, authored as text that renders to a diagram. The
  right form for structure / flow / dependency.
- **reveal.js decks** — assembled slides via the `presentation` toolkit (`deck`, `org-to-reveal`). The
  right form for a narrated, stepped presentation.

## The discipline
- **Emit a capturable artifact** — a diagram / deck is something a viewer (human, or a vision-modality
  agent) can reason over; prefer it to a wall of text for anything structural.
- **Compose, don't copy** — this skill composes the existing `toolkits/presentation` skill; don't
  re-implement the renderer.
- **Match the form to the content** — Mermaid for structure / flow, a deck for a narrated sequence.
